{"ts": 1784365924.4741936, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the full episode. After an early ~10pt adverse dip in the first minute, price snapped back and the leg ran strongly favorable for the rest of the window, peaking near +260pts with several deep-giveback pullbacks (up to ~85%) that each recovered rather than breaking through toward zero -- PROPP-with/HA-with kept re-firing on the bounces, confirming the thesis stayed intact. Never saw a sustained close below breakeven after frame 2, so no wrong-direction signature ever appeared to justify a bail. Next time I'd watch for a pullback that both breaches back near/below 0 AND coincides with a PROPP/HA-against fire plus rising ER10 (trending against) simultaneously -- that combination never occurred here, which is why this looked like a good trade that merely chopped rather than a wrong-direction entry.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 44}
